{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Live rich-text cutover + state echo suppression + concurrency conflict safety\n\n## Context / Problem\nCut the live Cloud and DC send paths over to the rich codecs (needs `e59d`, `271c`) and make\nthe cutover echo-safe. The DC codec is one-way and lossy, so\n`decode(encode(x))==x` cannot gate loops; both clients suppress echo by **state**, comparing\nthe current Jira value to the last-synced baseline (ADR 0026; `binding_store.get_baseline` `:447` /\n`set_baseline` `:450`; `_BASELINE_FIELDS` now lives in `peer_state.py:37`). Concurrency reuses story a713's local-wins\n+ deduped `outbound-field-conflict` alert.\n\n**Reused unchanged:** the ADR-0026/d6bd baseline diff (`binding_store.get_baseline` via `InboundMapper`,\n`outbound_field_diff.py:265`; `description` in `_INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS` `:47`, handled in\n`_compute_field_changes`); once-only re-emit convergence holds iff the codec\nlaw `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` holds (`test_rich_text_codec.py:163`,\na32a) plus marklas's 99.65% round-trip idempotence — hence no post-push GET;\n`_advance_baselines` (`reconcile_helpers.py:602`, `ctx.curr_snapshot`) as sole baseline\nwriter; comment dedup (`outbound_comments.py:48`) intact.\n\n## The live cutover\n- **Cloud:** repoint the four `AdfCodec` ops to `adf.py`'s Markdown-aware fns\n  (`to_wire→markdown_to_adf`, `decode_inbound→adf_to_markdown`,\n  `normalize_outbound→adf_to_markdown∘markdown_to_adf`,\n  `fit_outbound→fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`) + whole-codec plain-text fallback; update the pin\n  test (`test_rich_text_codec.py:198/205/207/208`). Reroute: encode\n  `adapters/jira/acli.py:209`, `acli_cli_ops.py:386`; fit `jira_fields.py:53`; compares\n  `adf.normalize_description`/`adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit` (`outbound_fields.py:586`,\n  `inbound_differ.py:210`) — **send-fit and compare-fit must be one transform**.\n- **DC:** `WikiTextCodec.to_wire` delegates to `wiki_render.render_markdown_to_wiki` (`271c`);\n  **redefine `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` to `decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`**, restoring the\n  codec law. DC's send composes `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))`\n  (`outbound_mapper.py:77`), so it ships rendered wiki on `issue.update(fields=…)`. **CREATE is\n  separate:** `_map_local_to_dc_fields` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:57`) builds its OWN\n  `WikiTextCodec()` and applies only `codec.fit_outbound(...)`, never `to_wire`, so it must\n  also render before the fit. Retarget the DC pin tests (`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`).\n- **Rollback:** a single config/flag switch restores the plain/identity path per client\n  without reverting codec capability; it **ships defaulting OFF**, enabled per client\n  (Cloud, then DC) after canary validation.\n\n## Design decisions\n1. **Two DISTINCT compares — do not collapse.** *Emit (`outbound_field_diff.py:288`),\n   local-vs-REMOTE — UNCHANGED:* `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(local))` vs\n   `canonical_remote[\"description\"]` = `decode_inbound(remote_wire)`\n   (`inbound_mapper.map_remote_to_local`); both decoded, so the lossy round-trip\n   cancels, and an un-normalized remote forces the one-time legacy upgrade re-emit\n   (`outbound_fields.py:586`). *Baseline (`_suppressed_by_inbound` `:323`,\n   `_local_matches_baseline` `:464`) — LOCAL side normalized:* raw local Markdown vs\n   `decode(baseline_wire)` differ in space, so a lossy codec reports \"local changed\"\n   each pass; route the local side through `RichTextCodec.normalize_outbound`\n   (`decode∘to_wire`, via `OutboundFieldMapper.map_fields_to_remote`) — the sole normalizer. `_remote_matches_baseline` (`:399`) — UNCHANGED.\n2. **Concurrent both-sides edit — unchanged.** When `local` and `remote`\n   both differ from `baseline`, `outbound_field_diff.py:450-457` appends `(jira_key, fname)` to\n   the `conflict_sink` and `run_differs.py:_emit_outbound_field_alerts` (`:97`) emits the\n   deduped alert; the emit stays local-wins and inbound keeps description **additive**\n   (`conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`/`_field_contract.FIELD_CONTRACT`, `resolve_additive`).\n3. **Shared-op side effect.** The `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` redefinition also\n   reaches the DC comment-diff dedup key (`outbound_comments._diff_comments` via `_resolve_codec:123`,\n   `:286`; `_IdentityCodec` docstring `:106-116`); that path keeps the identity/plain\n   normalizer UNCHANGED (rendering is `789c`'s).\n4. **Origin-gating + churn.** An update fires only when `local != baseline`, so a Jira-authored\n   construct (panel/mention/date, decoded by `adf.py` at `:164/219`) survives an edit-free\n   pass. Store a change-gated `rich_sha = sha256(rendered_wire)[:16]` (8 bytes) **inline** in\n   the binding (0.07 KB/version, the baseline profile; a per-pass timestamp reproduced\n   `0303`'s 12.62 KB anti-pattern); the compare never writes back.\n\n## Scope (IN)\n- `adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py` (+ fallback), `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`, the Cloud\n  consumer sites above and the `backend.py` (`:70`) CREATE path — gated.\n- `binding_store.py` inline `rich_sha`; `outbound_field_diff.py` (`:323`, `:464`) local-side\n  normalize only (`:292`/`:399`, `_advance_baselines`, `_apply_mutations` untouched);\n  `outbound_comments.py` untouched; tests under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`.\n\n## Scope (OUT)\n- No new three-way merge, LWW clock, conflict sink, or parallel `norm()`; no change to\n  `FIELD_CLASSES`/`_field_contract` or `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text`.\n- Comment rendering and the DC comment dedup-key migration (`789c`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cloud: a converted ADF description posts once; a second pass emits zero description\n  updates (`test_cloud_cutover_converges`).\n- [ ] DC: `issue.update(fields=…)` gets rendered wiki, not raw Markdown; a second pass emits\n  zero description updates (`test_dc_cutover_converges`).\n- [ ] TWO distinct compares kept: the emit compare stays on the plain inbound-decoded remote,\n  the LOCAL side of the baseline compares goes through `normalize_outbound` to match\n  `decode(baseline_wire)`; a no-edit body stays suppressed (zero re-emit) across passes, a\n  genuine rebar edit still shows changed, and a legacy body upgrades exactly once\n  then converges (`test_lossy_baseline_compare_local_normalized`,\n  `test_legacy_body_upgrades_once`, `test_lossy_body_converges_across_passes`).\n- [ ] The `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` redefinition leaves the DC comment-diff dedup key\n  unshifted, comment-diff converging with no duplicate re-post\n  (`test_dc_comment_diff_unchanged_by_cutover`).\n- [ ] Outbound fires only on a rebar-originated change (`local != baseline`), the baseline\n  advances via the existing `_advance_baselines`, and a benign re-canonicalization converges\n  in one re-emit without a re-GET (`test_echo_rebar_origin_only`,\n  `test_recanonicalization_converges`).\n- [ ] A Jira-authored construct (panel/mention/date) survives a later rebar pass under\n  origin-gating (`test_jira_native_construct_survives`).\n- [ ] A concurrent both-sides body edit keeps rebar's body (local-wins) AND raises the\n  existing `outbound-field-conflict` alert, so the remote value is recorded\n  (`test_concurrent_conflict_alerts`).\n- [ ] The rich layer stores an inline change-gated 8-byte `rich_sha`, no per-pass timestamp,\n  changing 0 entries on a no-op pass; verified by the git-delta harness at\n  ≤0.07 KB/version.\n- [ ] The cutover is flag-gated, ships defaulting OFF (opt-in per-client, not a 100%-traffic\n  flip) and reverts to the plain/identity wire when off (`test_cutover_defaults_off`,\n  `test_cutover_rollback_restores_plain`).\n- [ ] With the marklas extra absent, the cutover path emits the plain-text ADF wire (today's\n  behaviour) and raises nothing; verified by a test simulating the ImportError with the\n  cutover flag ON."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786596881865817001,"uuid":"d5be4945-999c-4ef4-b38d-3e9228f38e88"}